          "text": "Right lateral forefoot ulcer examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Near the fifth metatarsophalangeal joint; approximately 1.5 × 1.0 cm, depth to dermis, punched-out edges, pale base with yellow slough, minimal serous ooze, surrounding skin pale and slightly shiny. No significant erythema or warmth, no malodor, no exposed bone or tendon, no fluctuance, and no tracking cellulitis. Very tender on palpation and cleaning."
